 "_comment": "Low-poly fox head, 48 triangles, mirrored. A fox rather than a cat because the face tapers hard from pointed cheek ruffs into a long narrow snout. Eyes and nose are hatch-filled at 0.45 mm, below the 1.15 mm blot limit on purpose: inside an eye, solid is the goal. The mesh was cleaned with Lawson edge flips and one vertex removed, so no triangle has an angle under 19 degrees -- thinner slivers blot into dark wedges, which the server's drawing checks flag. The join block is what makes it draw correctly: supplied as triangles it would redraw every interior edge twice.",
